\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{The one-vertex Hurwitz model}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The \newvocab{one-vertex Hurwitz model} uses the
\vocabk{based cochains}{fdip-00SH} with #{n=2},
#{N_1=N_2=1}, scalar field #{\mathbb Q}, and coefficient
fiber #{F=\mathcal O\otimes_{\mathbb Z}\mathbb Q}.
The Hurwitz order and its #{24}-element unit group
#{G=2T} are those of \ref{fdip-00V1}. Write #{L_z(x)=zx}
for left multiplication on #{F}. A connection is an
ordered pair #{(U,V)\in G^2}, one unit on each positive
labeled loop at the vertex #{*}.}

\p{The cochain space
#{\mathcal V=\Lambda(\mathbb Q^2)\otimes_{\mathbb Q}F}
has one vertex slot, the two positive edge slots in directions
#{e_1,e_2}, and one face slot oriented by #{e_1\wedge e_2}.
Its ranks in degrees #{0,1,2} are #{4,8,4}, respectively, and
its total rank is #{16}. Distinct cell slots are orthogonal;
each carries the norm pairing
#{\langle x,y\rangle_0=\operatorname{Re}(\bar x y)}
of the \vocabk{Hurwitz fiber}{fdip-00V2}.}

\p{The inverse-link pullbacks are #{T_1=L_{U^{-1}}}
and #{T_2=L_{V^{-1}}}. For the
\vocabk{cochain operator}{fdip-00SR}, this gives
##{\begin{aligned}
\extd_{U,V}&=(e_1\wedge)(T_1-\bbI)
                 +(e_2\wedge)(T_2-\bbI),\\
\extdag_{U,V}&=(e_1\cdot)(T_1^{-1}-\bbI)
                 +(e_2\cdot)(T_2^{-1}-\bbI),\\
\extD_{U,V}&=\extd_{U,V}+\extdag_{U,V},\qquad
K_{U,V}(m)=m\bbI+\extD_{U,V}.
\end{aligned}}
Here #{m\in\mathbb Q}. The
\vocabk{coupled finite coefficient functional}{fdip-00TU}
has weight #{w(U,V)=1}, so its partition coefficient is
##{Z(m)=\sum_{(U,V)\in G^2}\det K_{U,V}(m).}
The sum counts all #{576} ordered pairs. Normalization
means division by #{Z(m)} only when it is nonzero.}
